        "DateText": "1527/30-1538?",
        "Notes": "Sources for the list of members of this Academy, are the following documents: the letter by Berni to Bini (Florence 12 April 1534), in Lettere facete et piacevoli ... raccolte da m. Dionigi Atanagi, libro primo (Venice: B. Zaltieri, 1561), p. 48; the dedication of Equicola Institutioni by Marco Sabino to Uberto Strozzi;  another letter by Mauro D`Arcano to Gandolfo Porrino (16 dic. 1531), in Lettere facete et piacevoli... (Venice: B. Zaltieri, 1561), pp. 319-323, See also Gianni Ballistreri, `Bini, Giovan Francesco`, in DBI, Paola Cosentino, `L`Accademia della Virtu`, dicerie e cicalate di Annibal Caro e di altri virtuosi`, in Cum notibusse et commentaribusse..., ed. Paolo Procaccioli, Manziana 2001, and Franco Pignatti, `Molza, Francesco Maria`, in DBI. Cosentino disagrees that Mauro`s letter to Porrino should be seen as a source related to this Academy.",
